[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
Documentation: https://sylve.io/docs/
Configuration: https://sylve.io/getting-started/#configuration-reference

Sylve provides many configurable settings and optional services. Review the
documentation before configuring and starting Sylve.

1) Review %%ETCDIR%%/config.json before starting Sylve. The built-in
   administrator username is "admin", and the supplied configuration sets
   its password to "admin". Change admin.password before starting the
   service for the first time. If you instead change it through the web
   interface, restrict access to trusted networks until the password has
   been changed under Settings > Authentication > Users > Local.

2) Sylve requires a configured system hostname.

3) Sylve stores runtime state under /var/db/sylve by default. Change
   dataPath in %%ETCDIR%%/config.json to use another location.

4) Enable Sylve with `sysrc sylve_enable=YES`, then start it with
   `service sylve start`.

5) Open https://HOST:8181 in a web browser.
EOM
}
{ type: upgrade
  maximum_version: "0.3.0"
  message: <<EOM
Documentation: https://sylve.io/docs/
Configuration: https://sylve.io/getting-started/#configuration-reference

Existing credentials are preserved during this upgrade. The built-in
administrator username is "admin". If its password is still "admin",
restrict Sylve to trusted networks until you change it through the web
interface under Settings > Authentication > Users > Local.

Alternatively, set admin.password to a strong value and
admin.forcePasswordReset to true in %%ETCDIR%%/config.json, then restart
Sylve.
EOM
}
]
